      "message": "The primary motivation for this is to add the move constructor for `AutoSTArray`, `trim_to`, and `kCount`. The other changes are right now for consistency and ease of testing.\n\nIn particular, `trim_to` and `kCount` allow for the user to \"allocate\" the whole storage (using `kCount`) to make it legal to pass the storage into interfaces which can optimistically take a buffer and fill it out if it is big enough (always returning the size of the buffer needed) and then use `trim_to` to shrink the allocation if necessary.",
